# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# Item 738 (steps/capture-738.md; Q38: nothing outside the copy is visible): the host `makeCounter`
# takes `Model: m` and returns the model `bump`, which reads and writes `m\value`.  The node carries a
# copy of `value` made at the return: the model's writes go to the copy -- the next call of the same
# node sees them (41, 42), the root's `left` does not (40) -- and a write of the root after the node is
# made is not seen by the node (43, not 100).  Success is 7; otherwise 16 plus a bit per failed reading:
# 1 and 2 the node's own calls, 4 the model's write seen by the root, 8 the root's write seen by the node
# -- so each side of the copy is read on its own.
Model:
    int: other 5
    int: value 40
end: Model

fn: makeCounter (Model: m) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: bump (int: x) int
        m\value: m\value + x
        return: m\value
    return: bump

Model: left
@: c makeCounter(left)
int: a (c: 1)
int: b (c: 1)
int: seen 0
seen: left\value
left\value: 99
int: d (c: 1)
int: bad 0
if: a != 41
    bad: bad + 1
if: b != 42
    bad: bad + 2
if: seen != 40
    bad: bad + 4
if: d != 43
    bad: bad + 8
int: ok 7
if: bad != 0
    ok: 16 + bad
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
